.TH VMCA 1 "April 2026" "vmca 3.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vmca \- VMM-side transparent vCPU pinning optimization tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vmca
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vmca
manages dynamic vCPU-to-pCPU pinning on the host (VMM) side, based on
pinning notifications from guest VMs. When a business application inside a
VM calls sched_setaffinity to pin to a specific vCPU, the guest-side
interceptor (kprobe or eBPF) detects this and notifies the VMM.
vmca then switches the corresponding vCPU from range-pinning to
1:1 exclusive pinning on a physical CPU. When the app un-pins, vmca
restores range-pinning.
.PP
VM vCPU pinning information is auto-discovered from libvirt using
.B virsh vcpupin <domain>
so no manual registration is required.  Each vCPU can have a different
CPU affinity range, which is read directly from the live VM configuration.
.PP
Based on patent: "一种优化虚拟机内业务绑核性能的方法" (Inventor: 张海亮).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B discover [\-\-vm \fINAME\fR]
Auto-discover running VMs and their per-vCPU pinning from libvirt
(via \fBvirsh vcpupin\fR).  If \fB\-\-vm\fR is given, only that VM is
discovered; otherwise all running VMs are discovered.
.TP
.B notify \-\-vm \fINAME\fR \-\-vcpu \fIID\fR \-\-action \fIpin|unpin\fR [\-\-pid \fIPID\fR]
Process a guest pinning notification (simulate or manual trigger).
.TP
.B status [\-\-vm \fINAME\fR] [\-\-format \fItable|json\fR]
Show vCPU pinning status for a specific VM or all VMs.
.TP
.B map [\-\-format \fItable|json\fR] [\-\-limit \fIN\fR]
Show the global CPU pinning map (all pCPU assignments).
.TP
.B unpin-all \-\-vm \fINAME\fR
Restore all vCPUs of a VM to range-pinning mode.
.TP
.B log [\-\-vm \fINAME\fR] [\-\-tail \fIN\fR]
Show recent pinning event log.
.TP
.B listen [\-\-dry-run]
Run the notification listener daemon. Auto-discovers all running VMs
on startup.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/vmca/global_cpu_map.json
Persistent global CPU mapping state.
